{"name":"Trench","hex":"#af9770","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Trench","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Telford, Telford and Wrekin borough, Shropshire, England .","A habitational surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Trench"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trench","blocks":[{"text":"A trench is a type of excavation or depression in the ground that is generally deeper than it is wide, and narrow compared with its length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Polyethylene_gas_main.jpg/330px-Polyethylene_gas_main.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trench"},{"title":"Trench (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Trench is the fifth studio album by the American musical duo Twenty One Pilots, released on October 5, 2018, through Fueled by Ramen and Elektra Records. It was the band's first studio album in three years, after the breakthrough success of their previous studio album, Blurryface (2015). Recorded in secret during a year-long public silence, it is a concept album which explores mental health, suicide, and doubt themes prominently featured in the band's previous works, framed in the metaphorical city of Dema and the surrounding continent known as \"Trench\". The album was also the first release of the newly revived Elektra Music Group."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Trench_Twenty_One_Pilots.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trench_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Atlantic-trench.JPG/500px-Atlantic-trench.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Atlantic-trench.JPG/1280px-Atlantic-trench.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_